WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.853
Ben looked down at his notes.

2
00:00:10.854 --> 00:00:14.758
"I have enough quotes about Mr. Freaky's sculpture," he thought.

3
00:00:14.759 --> 00:00:17.551
"I should probably interview the witches next."

4
00:00:17.552 --> 00:00:20.989
His article was due on Friday morning.

5
00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:24.324
Screech! A loud noise filled the hallway.

6
00:00:24.325 --> 00:00:25.349
"Watch out!"

7
00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:26.491
Ben looked up.

8
00:00:26.492 --> 00:00:29.407
He was pretty sure that was Pixel's voice.

9
00:00:29.408 --> 00:00:33.914
Crash! Boom! The zombies were now wide awake.

10
00:00:33.915 --> 00:00:38.258
"Wh-what is that thing?" a fish monster yelled.

11
00:00:38.259 --> 00:00:44.052
"It's Mr. Freaky's sculpture!" a blob said. "And it's alive!"

12
00:00:44.053 --> 00:00:45.751
Ben spun around.

13
00:00:45.752 --> 00:00:51.457
Sure enough, the massive sculpture had stopped spinning in place.

14
00:00:51.458 --> 00:00:55.346
Now it was rolling forward—right toward the crowd!

15
00:00:55.347 --> 00:00:59.254
"Run for your lives!" a werewolf howled.

16
00:00:59.255 --> 00:01:04.464
Students dived out of the way as the metal monster sputtered and screeched.

17
00:01:04.465 --> 00:01:09.605
Its parts spun and twisted.

18
00:01:09.606 --> 00:01:13.994
Ben shot backward as the sculpture rolled toward him.

19
00:01:13.995 --> 00:01:19.872
It rumbled closer and closer and then moved right through him!

20
00:01:19.873 --> 00:01:24.637
Crash! The sculpture smashed into the bank of lockers behind Ben.

21
00:01:24.638 --> 00:01:29.773
Everybody ducked as metal parts flew through the air.

22
00:01:29.774 --> 00:01:34.661
"Phew!" Ben gasped. "That was a close call!"

23
00:01:34.662 --> 00:01:38.994
Mr. Freaky ran down the hall and dropped to his knees.

24
00:01:38.995 --> 00:01:44.819
"My precious sculpture—it's ruined!"

25
00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:48.830
Ms. Van Ghoul hurried forward.

26
00:01:48.831 --> 00:01:52.458
"I'm sure you can piece it back together, Mr. Freaky." "But

27
00:01:52.459 --> 00:01:56.286
. . ." Mr. Freaky shook his head. "Isn't

28
00:01:56.287 --> 00:02:00.714
Leonardo da Creepy coming tomorrow?" "Yes,"

29
00:02:00.715 --> 00:02:03.244
Ms. Van Ghoul said. "He

30
00:02:03.245 --> 00:02:07.556
wants to make sure that our art is up to his artistic standards. It's

31
00:02:07.557 --> 00:02:09.518
just a quick inspection. He'll

32
00:02:09.519 --> 00:02:12.730
be back on Friday night for the big event." Mr.

33
00:02:12.731 --> 00:02:16.435
Freaky gave a heavy sigh. "I

34
00:02:16.436 --> 00:02:20.559
wanted him to see Moving Inspiration while he was here. But

35
00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:23.237
I guess it can wait." He

36
00:02:23.238 --> 00:02:28.204
picked up a twisted metal pipe and stared at it gloomily. "My

37
00:02:28.205 --> 00:02:33.377
sculpture was working fine this morning," he muttered. "I

38
00:02:33.378 --> 00:02:37.285
think somebody sabotaged it!" Mr.

39
00:02:37.286 --> 00:02:43.926
Freaky started gathering up the broken pieces of Moving Inspiration .

40
00:02:43.927 --> 00:02:49.201
Meanwhile Ms. Van Ghoul waved some students over to a quiet spot.

41
00:02:49.202 --> 00:02:53.728
Until now, the art teacher hadn’t seemed bothered by the vandalism.

42
00:02:53.729 --> 00:02:58.085
This time, however, Ben thought she looked worried.

43
00:02:58.086 --> 00:03:06.410
"Leonardo da Creepy is a famous artist," Ms. Van Ghoul began, "and he's very, very picky.

44
00:03:06.411 --> 00:03:09.807
We cannot let any other problems happen this week.

45
00:03:09.808 --> 00:03:13.844
Otherwise, Mr. da Creepy might not participate."

46
00:03:13.845 --> 00:03:19.103
A goblin gasped. "But he's supposed to give us a new painting!"

47
00:03:19.104 --> 00:03:23.450
"Yeah. It could be another Moaning Lisa ," a blob

48
00:03:23.451 --> 00:03:28.082
added. "A painting like that could make Monster Academy

49
00:03:28.083 --> 00:03:31.871
famous!" "I know." Ms. Van Ghoul nodded in

50
00:03:31.872 --> 00:03:37.805
agreement. "I've spent a lot of time convincing him to come here to celebrate Art Week with

51
00:03:37.806 --> 00:03:41.329
us. It would be awful if he

52
00:03:41.330 --> 00:03:50.684
canceled. So if you know anything about who is causing all the trouble, please tell me

53
00:03:50.685 --> 00:03:56.364
immediately." Ben looked down, wondering if he should say something about the trail of paint drops in the

54
00:03:56.365 --> 00:03:59.871
gym. It was a clue—maybe even a big

55
00:03:59.872 --> 00:04:03.552
clue. But a part of him was still worried that Mog was

56
00:04:03.553 --> 00:04:07.168
involved. Ben didn’t want his friend to get in

57
00:04:07.169 --> 00:04:10.317
trouble. "I won’t say anything yet," Ben

58
00:04:10.318 --> 00:04:17.306
thought. If he kept interviewing monsters and teachers for his story, he might learn more about what was going

59
00:04:17.307 --> 00:04:20.294
on. Suddenly he had an

60
00:04:20.295 --> 00:04:24.923
idea. Pixel had been taking a ton of photos all week

61
00:04:24.924 --> 00:04:29.125
long. Maybe his camera held some

62
00:04:29.126 --> 00:04:32.939
clues. Ben darted off, looking for

63
00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:41.435
Pixel. As he flew past the art room, he saw Mog and the Doppel Gang in there, helping the mummies make the

64
00:04:41.436 --> 00:04:46.310
pyramids. Ben felt a wave of relief. "That's good," he thought.

65
00:04:46.311 --> 00:04:50.734
"It looks like Mog has been too busy to mess with Mr. Freaky's sculpture."

66
00:04:50.735 --> 00:04:54.872
"Has anyone seen Pixel?" Ben called into the classroom.

67
00:04:54.873 --> 00:04:58.474
They all shook their heads. "No."

68
00:04:58.475 --> 00:05:00.979
"Thanks."

69
00:05:00.980 --> 00:05:05.568
Ben's next stop was the newspaper office.

70
00:05:05.569 --> 00:05:08.036
"There you are!" Ben said.

71
00:05:08.037 --> 00:05:16.244
Pixel sat at a desk, staring at his camera with a worried expression.

72
00:05:16.245 --> 00:05:19.176
"Are you okay?"

73
00:05:19.177 --> 00:05:22.598
"No." Pixel shook his head.

74
00:05:22.599 --> 00:05:25.605
"Something happened to my camera.

75
00:05:25.606 --> 00:05:29.753
It went dead as soon as Mr. Freaky's sculpture stopped moving."

76
00:05:29.754 --> 00:05:31.495
He bit his lip.

77
00:05:31.496 --> 00:05:34.074
"It seems to be working again now.

78
00:05:34.075 --> 00:05:37.518
But most of the photos I took are gone."

79
00:05:37.519 --> 00:05:39.795
"What?" Ben's heart sank.

80
00:05:39.796 --> 00:05:45.035
He needed those photos for his article—not to mention his investigation.

81
00:05:45.036 --> 00:05:47.399
"Don't worry," Pixel said quickly.

82
00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:52.471
"As long as my camera is working, I can take some more photos today and tomorrow.

83
00:05:52.472 --> 00:05:56.391
I'll have plenty for the story and the school website."

84
00:05:56.392 --> 00:06:00.117
"Okay." Ben nodded, hoping Pixel was right.

85
00:06:00.118 --> 00:06:02.552
"Sounds good. Thanks.

86
00:06:02.553 --> 00:06:06.916
In the meantime Mr. Freaky wants me to find out what happened with his sculpture.

87
00:06:06.917 --> 00:06:11.360
Did you happen to notice anything suspicious while you were taking photos?"

88
00:06:11.361 --> 00:06:18.012
"Nope," Pixel said. "Sorry, but I didn't see a thing."

